{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Elohim went up from upon him</b> — as it says regarding Abraham (Genesis 17:22), \"And Elohim went up from upon Abraham.\" In both of them this is to make known that this was not merely a vision and a prophetic dream alone, or like the matter of \"and He brought me to Jerusalem in visions of Elohim\" (Ezekiel 8:3), but rather that the Shekhinah rested upon him in the place where he was standing. And by way of truth, Elohim went up from upon him in the place that was speaking with him, like the matter that is said, \"Blessed be the glory of YHWH from His place\" (ibid. 3:12). And one may say that which the Sages mentioned: the Patriarchs are the Merkavah (Genesis Rabbah 82:6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:37.235206001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}